                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kamat",
                        "email": "deepakkamat6630@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkamat27"
                    },
                    "message": "tried to simulate the stress on the uart terminal by writing - yes \"UART load test\" > /dev/ttyAMA0 and the interrupts capture those so similarly in the situation where network is under stress we should be able to get this under 2 or 3 dump data which can be useful for the hardware issue debug and faults.\n\nroot@qemuarm:/tmp# cat /proc/interrupts\n           CPU0\n 26:     380065 GIC-0  27 Level     arch_timer\n 28:       1576 GIC-0  33 Level     uart-pl011\n \n root@qemuarm:/tmp# cat /proc/interrupts\n           CPU0\n 26:     390951 GIC-0  27 Level     arch_timer\n 28:       1642 GIC-0  33 Level     uart-pl011"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Milton D. Miller II",
                        "email": "mdmii@outlook.com",
                        "username": "mdmillerii"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm fine with collecting these.   but I caution this just represents the total count since boot to the point of dump collection.    comparison of 2 or more points ideally before and after is often required unless you see 1000000 or whatever the the threshold for a stuck interrupt.\n\nI have used these in my kernel debug, and it's useful for none/handful/lots and balance between cores.\n\nalso network and possibly storage can switch to adaptive polling when expecting a steady stream of traffic.   UART often have 16-256 characters per interrupt and may or may not differentiate between rx and tx."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
